			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Regenerate build artifacts and route manifest\n\nExecute a full build of the Cocoon extension host sidecar to capture the latest state of the codebase. This commit updates the generated `RouteManifest` timestamps and recompiles all TypeScript sources to JavaScript, including the gRPC server, request handlers, and VS Code API adapters.\n\nThe build artifacts in the `Target/` directory are updated to reflect the current directory casing conventions and ensure the `RouteManifest` accurately reflects the 118 available Mountain methods. Source maps are regenerated for all modules to support debugging.",
			"SHA": "8c9707c343cce9e2f5d2d2db15ff33ec994621ed"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T16:17:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1137,
				69
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Normalize gRPC directory casing and update references\n\nRename `GRPC` directories to `gRPC` within `Source/Services` to align with the standard mixed-case abbreviation convention used throughout the codebase. Update all internal imports in `Service`, `RPCServer`, `Window`, `Workspace`, `Command`, and `Mapping` to reflect the new path structure.\n\nAdditionally, standardize the `TierRemoteProcedureCallValue` type and default configuration strings from `\"GRPC\"` to `\"gRPC\"`. Regenerate the `RouteManifest` to account for the new repository state, which adds 27 language feature provider methods to the `MountainMethods` set.\n\nThis ensures consistency in directory naming conventions and corrects case sensitivity in all IPC-related module references.",
			"SHA": "a44df478863b41041c3f6ce5fb464fe7a7b184c0"
		},
